# Trials of Atlantis and Catacombs as rumours only (owner, 2026-11-15, "Yes agreed on lore"). Nobody in this world has been
# to a sunken land or under a capital, nobody has master levels, artifacts or a Catacombs class, and no line suggests the
# player can go. Atlantis is sailors' and grandmothers' talk; what lies under the capitals is a door that stays shut.
#
# The tag: @topic rumour_atlantis or rumour_below. Only lines with that topic may say "atlantis" or "catacombs"
# (tools/bot-voices/build_corpus.py, ERA_RUMOUR_TOPICS); every other out-of-era word stays banned in them too.
# Where they are heard (rare by design):
#   - the storyteller's legend of the glass that spoke (topic tale_atlantis, AutonomousTales.Legends), in the tale rotation;
#   - one /faction debate (an ordinary scene, one of several hundred);
#   - a few place-bound /faction musings (AutonomousChatFiller: musings are a 5% share of /faction openers, one written
#     line per realm in 20 minutes);
#   - answers when a player asks ("what is atlantis", "is there anything under camelot", LoreLegends).
# New writing; Mythic's lore (camelotherald.com/node/244) paraphrased, never quoted.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the storyteller's legend: the glass that spoke
@kind debate
@realm *
@topic tale_atlantis
@levels 1-50
@scene tale_atlantis
@role A type=*
@role B type=*
@role C type=Socialite,Explorer
@role D type=*
@role E type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role F type=Leveler,Crafter,Explorer
A: {name_b} you on? tell the glass ball one | {name_b}, do your gran's story. the orb
C: oh this one. hush all | quiet everyone, {name_b} is doing the orb
?E: the talking ball again lol | here we go, the ball that talks
D: please {name_b}, i never heard it | go on {name_b}, the new ones dont know it
B: its my family's story, so no correcting me
B: my gran's gran poured the cups at the council hall
B: one winter a fisherman came up from the coast with a wet sack. his net had come up heavy
B: in it was a ball of glass the size of a baby's head. warm. coral grown over one side
B: the council paid him two coins to go away and set it on the high table like a pudding
~ 8
D: and then it talked? | so when does it talk?
B: the eighth night, candles low. a light came up inside it, like a lamp seen through water
B: in the light stood a man no bigger than her thumb, in robes nobody here ever wore
B: he said past the edge of the sea is a land where peoples are tried. ten trials, one for each thing worth being
B: send your champions, he said. the ones who pass come home more than they were
?F: did they send anyone? | so who went?
B: they argued till dawn. then he said it all again. same words, same pause in the same place
B: he never once looked at them. thats when she went cold
B: she dreamed for years after. sand to the end of the world. a mountain on fire. a city sat on a cloud
B: and the sky cracking like pond ice, and the sea standing up, and all of it gone in a day and a night
B: in spring they sewed it back in the sack and rowed it out past the point
B: she was in the boat. she said it was still talking when it went under
~ 25
F: ...still talking | wait. still talking?
A: ty {name_b}. not going near the docks tonight | thanks {name_b}. i will never fish again
@end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- a /faction debate: the uncle's city
@kind debate
@realm *
@topic rumour_atlantis
@levels 1-50
@scene rumour_atlantis_uncle
@role A type=Socialite,Explorer
@role B type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role C type=*
@role D type=*
A: {q} my uncle says theres a whole city under the sea lol
B: your uncle also said he soloed the dragon
A: he said that once. but the fishermen really do drag up carved stone, crusted in coral
C: the sailors even have a name for it. atlantis | harbour folk call it atlantis. they get quiet about it
?D: so what are the lights out past the harbour at night? | then what are the lights under the water
B: fish that glow. or your uncle with a lantern
A: laugh all you like. somebody will row out there one day and come back with proof
B: and your uncle will say he was there first
@end

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- answers: "what is atlantis?" (LoreLegends)
@kind reply
@topic rumour_atlantis
@answers ask_atlantis
@realm alb
@about place
[harbour talk|sailor talk] from caer gothwaite. a land past the isles that sank in one day and one night. nobody has been
@realm mid
aegirhamn sailor talk. a drowned land past the isles. buy one an ale and you get it twice
@realm hib
the boatmen at the domnann dock [talk about it|swear by it]. a sunk land out west. none of them has rowed out to look

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- answers: "is there anything under the city?"
@kind reply
@topic rumour_below
@answers ask_below
@realm alb
@about place
old crypts under camelot, bricked up. the cellar folk say the inconnu never had to ask the way down
@realm mid
kobold miners swear theres a city under jordheim. they hear picks [below|under] their own picks
@realm hib
the dream tree roots under tnn go down further than roots should. the druids stopped following them

